cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this register, please cite it as below. Verify any grant against its linked land case before citing the grant itself."
title: "Ranchos of California: A Register of the Land Grants of Alta California"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Coyne
    given-names: Aodhan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8630-3768"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22185500
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aodhanm/ranchos-portal"
url: "https://ranchos.archivesofcalifornia.com/"
abstract: >-
  A structured register of the 672 documented land grants made in Alta
  California under Spanish and Mexican rule, 1769 to 1846, each joined to
  its United States land case, to the federal patent that closed the case,
  and, where one exists, to the Supreme Court opinion that decided it.
  Fields cover grantee, granting governor and era, acreage in acres and
  square leagues, county, land case docket, final disposition, patentee,
  patent date and acreage, General Land Office patent number, and a deep
  link to the digitized land case file at the Bancroft Library. Compiled
  from the Bancroft land case files, the Online Archive of California
  finding aid, Perez (1982), Hoffman (1862), and the General Land Office
  patent record.
keywords:
  - California history
  - land grants
  - ranchos
  - Mexican California
  - Spanish borderlands
  - land tenure
  - public land survey
  - digital humanities
